{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghTr78zHutEESS6nimwf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq ≈ 1070 cm⁻¹ and B ≈ 862 cm⁻¹, with 10Dq ≈ 10 700 cm⁻¹. This is a high-spin d⁷ (Co²⁺-type) complex with a ⁴T₁g ground term.\n\n**Assignment of the bands**\n- 9 460 cm⁻¹ is ν₁, ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴T₂g.\n- 20 160 cm⁻¹ is ν₂, ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴A₂g.\n- 21 160 cm⁻¹ is ν₃, ⁴T₁g(F) → ⁴T₁g(P).\n\n**Dq from the band spacing**\n- ν₂ − ν₁ = 10Dq, which is 20 160 − 9 460 = 10 700 cm⁻¹.\n- This gives Dq ≈ 1070 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B from the ν₃ assignment**\n- A simple two-term analysis of the ⁴T₁g(F)/⁴T₁g(P) mixing, using only ν₁ and ν₂, gives B ≈ 800 cm⁻¹. It then puts ν₃ near 26 700 cm⁻¹, far from the observed 21 160 cm⁻¹. So that shortcut does not describe this spectrum.\n- I therefore used the `ts_fit_spectrum` tool, which diagonalises the full d⁷ matrix, to fit all three bands. It gave Dq = 1069.7 cm⁻¹ and B = 862 cm⁻¹.\n- The fit reproduces the bands at 9 462, 20 159 and 21 160 cm⁻¹, with residuals of about 1–2 cm⁻¹.\n- B = 862 cm⁻¹ is about 89% of the free-ion value for Co²⁺ (≈ 970 cm⁻¹), so the nephelauxetic reduction is modest.\n\n**Racah C**\n- The spin-allowed bands do not constrain C. The 4499 cm⁻¹ the tool reports is only its default, so I am not reporting a fitted C.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1070, \"B\": 862, \"C\": null, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Full d7 matrix fit of the three spin-allowed bands gives Dq≈1070 and B≈862 cm^-1 (rmse ~1 cm^-1); C is not constrained by these bands.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3153,"cache_read_input_tokens":7985,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3153,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":